+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:20:04 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 177/222] firmware: qcom: scm: add QSEECom app shutdown
+
+TZ refuses to load an application that is already loaded, and nothing released
+one, so re-initialising meant rebooting. That matters because an application
+asks the normal world for its stored state during a first initialisation and
+never again, so anything that changes what it is served cannot be re-tested
+without a fresh load.
+
+The app manager service has a shutdown command at 2, between start at 1 and
+lookup at 3. Verified on an SM8250: with 'gfenu' resident and a load returning
+-EINVAL, issuing owner 50 / service 1 / command 2 with the app id returned
+success and echoed the id back in the response data, and the next load
+succeeded.
