new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..0b5f4bee21
--- /dev/null
+++ b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/0178-tee-qseecom-unload-an-application-when-its-load-sess.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:20:05 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 178/222] tee: qseecom: unload an application when its load
+ session closes
+
+The driver already knows which applications it loaded, and a load session on
+the privileged device owns the application it started, so closing that session
+is the natural place to release it. Without this, TZ keeps the application
+until reboot and refuses to load it again.
+
+Sessions on the client device are unaffected -- they reference an application,
+they do not own it.
+
+A failing shutdown is warned about and leaves the registry entry alone, so the
+worst case is the previous behaviour.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
+(cherry picked from commit 912c8192953079002d1ee8c301dd41135b8f088b)
+---
+ drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
+ 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
