+ moved on
+
+A supplicant that overruns the ten-second timeout comes back to find its
+request abandoned, and possibly a different one already in the slot. Nothing
+distinguished the two, so the late answer was applied to whichever request was
+outstanding -- handing one application the reply meant for another. Since a
+bogus success is what leaves the secure world acting on a buffer that was never
+filled, that is the worst available outcome.
+
+Stamp each posted request with a generation, record the one the supplicant took,
+and reject a send whose generation has moved on.
+
