+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 11:05:39 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 200/222] tee: qseecom: allocate through the core's dynamic shm
+ helper
+
+The pool's alloc and free were a near-copy of tee_dyn_shm_alloc_helper() and
+tee_dyn_shm_free_helper() -- same page rounding, same alloc_pages_exact() with
+__GFP_ZERO, same virt_to_phys(), same free_pages_exact(). OP-TEE and tstee both
+use the helper; there is no reason for a third copy.
+
+Passing NULL for the registration callback says what is true here: nothing is
+registered with the secure world, because this memory is never handed to it.
+The flag is cleared for the same reason, as tee_shm_pool_alloc_res_mem() does.
+
+The reasoning about cacheability and page rounding is kept -- it is the part
+that is not obvious.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
+Assisted-by: Kimi:kimi-k3
+(cherry picked from commit 734e28e28577c1bd37bb4e69db3d496766ccdfc6)
