+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:00:16 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 205/222] tee: qseecom: drop every parameter's reference before
+ refusing a receive
+
+The core resolves any memref passed to TEE_IOC_SUPPL_RECV and takes a
+reference for it, leaving the driver to drop them. Rejecting a non-empty
+parameter from inside the same loop that drops them returns before visiting
+the rest, so the references of every parameter after the offending one are
+stranded. A leaked tee_shm reference pins the context, which strands the
+device on unregister.
+
+Drop them all first, then validate.
+
+Reported-by: Kimi K3
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
