+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:00:49 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 206/222] tee: qseecom: allow one receiver, not one opener, on
+ the supplicant device
+
+Rejecting a second open of the privileged device enforced the single-supplicant
+rule in the wrong place. Loading an application is an open_session on that same
+device, so a supplicant holding it open made every load fail with -EBUSY --
+including the documented flow of starting the file service and then loading the
+application it serves.
+
+The constraint is really about who consumes requests, so enforce it there: the
+first context to receive claims the role, and a receive or send from any other
+context is refused. Opening the device stays free.
+
+The role is released when its context closes, and an in-flight request is
+abandoned then too, which previously happened only once the last opener went
+away -- with a loader also holding the device open, that could have left a
+request unanswered until the loader closed.
+
