+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:01:19 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 207/222] tee: qseecom: bind a supplicant's answer to the
+ request it took
+
+The generation check in the send path could never fire. taken_gen is assigned
+from req_gen at the moment a request is taken, and req_gen only advances where
+taken is cleared, so for as long as a request is taken the two are equal by
+construction and the -ESTALE branch was unreachable. The hole it was meant to
+close stayed open: a supplicant that overran the timeout, whose request was
+abandoned and replaced, could still answer, and its stale success would be
+applied to the new request with the reply buffer never filled -- which is the
+observed way to hang the secure world.
+
+A counter the kernel never shows anyone cannot do this, because the answer
+carries nothing to compare against. Hand it out instead: RECV now returns the
+generation in a VALUE_OUTPUT and SEND takes it back in a VALUE_INPUT, the shape
+OP-TEE settled on for the same problem. Comparing the echoed value against
+req_gen makes the rejection real.
+
+While here, clear pending when a request is taken rather than only when it
+completes. A second thread receiving on the same fd would otherwise see pending
+still set, return from the wait immediately, find the request taken, and spin
+at full CPU taking the supplicant mutex every iteration.
+
