new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..bdf39923fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/0220-input-misc-add-Goodix-SPI-fingerprint-sensor-driver.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,796 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:20:29 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 220/222] input: misc: add Goodix SPI fingerprint sensor driver
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+Goodix ships one downstream driver for these sensors, and it covers two
+arrangements: the operating system images the sensor over SPI itself, or a
+secure-world trusted application does it and the operating system never touches
+that bus. Only the second is implemented here — the sources this is derived
+from carry no SPI transfers at all — so the driver is named for the part it
+serves rather than for that arrangement, leaving room for the other.
+
+It controls the platform hardware resources the operating system owns in either
+case — the supply, the reset line and the interrupt — and exposes the interfaces
+a userspace client needs:
+
+- the /dev/goodix_fp character device with the GF_IOC_* ioctl ABI
+  (reset, irq enable/disable, power, key/nav event injection)
+- a netlink socket that reports sensor interrupts
+- the "uinput-goodix" input device for key and navigation events
+- firmware-name read from the device tree, reported at /sys/.../firmware_name,
+  so a client can learn which trusted application drives the sensor (application
+  is typically unique to the hardware platform)
+
+Derived from the downstream Goodix driver (Xiaomi msm-5.4 / lineage-22.2,
+drivers/input/fingerprint/goodix/, platform-bus variant), which Goodix ships
+across parts and handsets, with:
+
+- support for capacity touch (side-mounted) sensor only; support for the
+  under-screen optical reader was dropped with no hardware to test it. As a
+  result, the Xiaomi DRM blank notifier and its FB_BLACK/FB_UNBLACK netlink
+  events were not carried over. That path tells the trusted application whether
+  the panel is lit, which an in-display optical sensor requires because the panel
+  illuminates the finger. These can, however, be ported at later time, provided
+  support can be tested at compatible hardware
+- the gpiod API for reset, a standard interrupt taken with platform_get_irq(),
+  and a regular "vdd" regulator acquired once at probe, where downstream did
+  regulator_get/put on every open
+- miscdevice in place of the manual chrdev, class and minor-bitmap boilerplate;
+  the device node path is unchanged
+- usleep_range() for the short reset pulse and settle delay. msleep() under
+  20 ms can sleep considerably longer than asked, which is the wrong instrument
+  for a hardware timing; the ftrace-style entry logging in the interrupt handler
+  went with it
+- the dead AP_CONTROL_CLK, GF_FASYNC and GF_PW_CTL variants and the redundant
+  access_ok() checks removed
+- single-user open enforcement, downstream having re-requested the GPIOs and
+  IRQ on every open so that a second open failed regardless
+- a void remove callback, devm allocations and checkpatch cleanup
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
+Signed-off-by: Dawid Wróbel <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+(cherry picked from commit 0e58919b031cb9bd3f6d4820c976172640bc672e)
+---
+ drivers/input/misc/Kconfig         |  17 +
+ drivers/input/misc/Makefile        |   1 +
+ drivers/input/misc/goodix_fp_spi.c | 687 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
+ 3 files changed, 705 insertions(+)
+ create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/goodix_fp_spi.c
+
+diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig b/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig
+index fa92671197..d23c79c271 100644
+--- a/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig
++++ b/drivers/input/misc/Kconfig
+@@ -247,6 +247,23 @@ config INPUT_PMIC8XXX_PWRKEY
+ 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+ 	  module will be called pmic8xxx-pwrkey.
+ 
++config INPUT_GOODIX_FP_SPI
++	tristate "Goodix SPI fingerprint sensor driver"
++	depends on INPUT && OF_GPIO && NET
++	help
++	  Say Y here to enable the driver for Goodix SPI fingerprint
++	  sensors. It controls the sensor supply, reset and interrupt
++	  lines, and exposes the /dev/goodix_fp ioctl and netlink ABI the
++	  fingerprint HAL expects.
++
++	  Only sensors driven by a TrustZone application are currently
++	  supported. Their SPI bus belongs to the secure world, which
++	  captures and matches fingerprints there. Sensors the operating
++	  system drives itself need SPI transfers this driver does not
++	  currently implement.
++
++	  If unsure, say N.
++
+ config INPUT_SPARCSPKR
+ 	tristate "SPARC Speaker support"
+ 	depends on PCI && SPARC64
